<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arghun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1258–<a href="/years/1291">1291</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arghun was the fourth Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, reigning from 1284 to 1291. He came to power by overthrowing his uncle Tekuder, and he sent several embassies to the pope and the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> seeking an alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> he executed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-ii-nicator">Demetrius II</a> in 1289 and treated the kingdom as a dependent territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arghun.jpg" alt="Arghun" width="287" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sayf al-Vâhidî · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ArghunEnthroned_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1290 the Ilkhan <b>Arghun</b> told Pope Nicholas IV that whoever prays to Eternal Tengri with righteous thoughts has done as much as if he had received baptism.</blockquote><a href="/religion/tengrism">Tengrism · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Arghuns</b>, Turko-Mongol nobles who had served the Timurid rulers of Herat, held Kandahar until Babur drove them out in the 1510s.</blockquote><a href="/state/arghun-dynasty">Arghun dynasty</a></li><li><blockquote>Jam Nizam al-Din, known as Jam Nindo, ruled for more than four decades around 1461 to 1508 and is remembered as a just and pious ruler who defended Sindh against the <b>Arghuns</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/samma-dynasty">Samma dynasty</a></li><li><blockquote>Mirza Isa Tarkhan, an officer of the Arghun dynasty descended from a Mongol military family, seized Thatta in 1554 as <b>Arghun</b> authority collapsed.</blockquote><a href="/state/tarkhan-dynasty">Tarkhan dynasty</a></li></ul></section>
